{
 "about": "How pipeline/rig_onto_host.py fits The Pack (Dead Space 2 child necromorph, skeleton 'pack', 49 joints) onto a Vermintide 2 Skaven rat skeleton (j_* joints, e.g. skaven_slave). Unnamed DS2 joints keep their rcb index: bone_04/bone_07 spine, bone_11 back, bone_21 head, bone_23/24 upper arms, bone_27/28 wrist twists, bone_01 ground marker. Same fields as slasher_to_vt2_human.json.",
 "fields": {
  "weights": "host joint that gets this bone's vertex weights. If that host does not link it (pipeline/bones/<breed>.txt), rig_onto_host.py uses a linked child at the same spot, else the nearest linked parent. A list gives alternatives for hosts without the first joint (rats: j_neck_1, j_jaw, no _roll joints); the first one the host has is used",
  "head": "fit: move the bone's head to this host joint (or [joint_a, joint_b, t] = point between them)",
  "stretch": "fit: stretch the bone so its tail reaches this host joint (changes the bone's length)",
  "aim": "fit: turn the bone towards this host joint without changing its length",
  "tail_to": "before fitting, point the bone's tail at this DS2 bone's head, so stretch/aim use the limb's real direction",
  "rigid": "true: keep this part's own size even if its parent is stretched (heads, hands, blades)"
 },
